DESCRIPTION >
    Edge-case check: count of events with an AI source but no UTM source (any
    event type). Tenant-scoped; prunes via site_id (this query has no
    timestamp predicate — preserved exactly from source). Faithful 1:1 port of
    api/routes/events.js:312-320 (queryName 'edge_ai_no_utm'). Typed-column
    translation: properties.site_id -> site_id, properties.ai_source ->
    ai_source (typed, LowCardinality Nullable per §2.6), properties.utm_source
    -> utm_source (typed, Nullable per §2.6). No JSON-bag fields.
    NOT YET PUSHED — validated read-only via `tb --cloud sql` only.
    COST FINDING (Task 1, Phase 6 consolidation pass): checked the LIVE source at
    api/routes/events.js:301-330 verbatim — the live HogQL query genuinely has
    NO timestamp predicate either (confirmed at HEAD, not assumed). This is
    NOT a port bug; the app itself scans the tenant's entire event history
    for this check, unbounded. Faithful-port rule means NOT adding a bound
    here — that would diverge from live behavior and break parity. Accepted
    cost characteristic, documented rather than silently carried: on the
    deployed endpoint (`tb --cloud endpoint data edge_ai_no_utm --site_id ...`),
    rows_read = 45 for the gating site's current (small) history; this
    number scales with the site's LIFETIME event volume, not a bounded
    recent window, and will grow as sites age. FLAGGED for later, not fixed
    now (would require an app-caller change, out of scope for this
    pipe-only pass): add a caller-side date param (e.g. trailing 90d) once
    events.js is wired to call this pipe instead of live HogQL — that
    caller-side change is deferred with the rest of the app-coupling work
    per the standing rule for this batch.

NODE edge_ai_no_utm_node
SQL >
    %
    SELECT count() AS cnt
    FROM events
    WHERE site_id = {{ String(site_id, required=True) }}
      AND ai_source IS NOT NULL
      AND ai_source != ''
      AND (utm_source IS NULL OR utm_source = '')

TYPE endpoint
